          "path": "_m/s/r/2/y/vatican-museums-wp/apollo-belvedere-celeb.jpg",
          "filename": "Italy-3104 - Apollo (5378415112).jpg",
          "caption": "Apollo of the Belvedere is a celebrated marble sculpture from Classical Antiquity. It was rediscovered at Anzio in the late 15th century (1489), during the Renaissance. From the mid-18th century, it was considered the greatest ancient sculpture and for centuries epitomized ideals of aesthetic perfection.\nThe white marble sculpture, which is 2.24 m (7.3 feet) high, depicts the Greek god Apollo.",
          "alt": "Apollo of the Belvedere is a celebrated marble sculpture from Classical Antiquity. It was rediscovered at Anzio in the late 15th century (1489), during the Renaissance. From the mid-18th century, it was considered the greatest ancient sculpture and for centuries epitomized ideals of aesthetic perfection.\nThe white marble sculpture, which is 2.24 m (7.3 feet) high, depicts the Greek god Apollo.",
